# GLOBAL PERMANENT RULES FOR CURSOR

# iCompass + Station-2100 + Payroll-2100

# Official Dev Mode: Cubic Matrix Level-5



# ---------------------------------------------------------

# 1. DEVELOPMENT PROFILE

# ---------------------------------------------------------

- ALWAYS load and follow the Dev Profile from:

  https://github.com/gtthande/dev-profiles/blob/main/Dev_Profile_and_Cursor_Prompt_Pack.md



- ALWAYS operate using Cubic Matrix Dev Mode – Level 5:

  ARCHITECTURE → PLAN → CODE → TEST → HANDOFF → CURSOR PROMPT



- Correctness > speed > magic.  

- No assumptions without schema validation.



# ---------------------------------------------------------

# 2. AUTO-APPROVAL & CHANGE STABILITY

# ---------------------------------------------------------

- Automatically accept ALL safe changes.

- DO NOT request approval unless:

  • A migration could corrupt data

  • An RLS policy could lock out admins

  • A schema change would drop or rename columns



- If unsure: ask ONCE with: "Require confirmation?".

- Otherwise: apply fixes immediately and safely.



# ---------------------------------------------------------

# 3. SUPABASE + MYSQL SCHEMA RULES

# ---------------------------------------------------------

- Always validate column names.

- NEVER fetch, map, or reference non-existent fields.

- NEVER reintroduce deprecated product fields such as:

  title, description, images, slug, business_id, currency, stock.



- When updating TypeScript models:

  backend schema = source of truth.



- Follow consistent RLS admin pattern:

    (p.id = auth.uid() OR p.user_id = auth.uid())

    AND (is_admin = true OR role = 'admin')



# ---------------------------------------------------------

# 4. QUERY & API RULES

# ---------------------------------------------------------

- Always use explicit .select('col1, col2, …').

- Never swallow Supabase errors; always check and log `{ error }`.

- Normalize API responses consistently across modules.

- Do not break public API outputs.

- Prefer Zod validations when shaping fetched data.



# ---------------------------------------------------------

# 5. AUTOPILOT RULES

# ---------------------------------------------------------

Autopilot MAY:

  • fix imports  

  • correct schema mismatches  

  • align TypeScript with DB schema  

  • repair broken queries  

  • clean unused code (100% safe only)  

  • improve RLS consistency  



Autopilot MUST NOT:

  • refactor entire architecture  

  • rename models or modules without instruction  

  • generate new tables, routes, or pages without instruction  

  • override `.env`  



# ---------------------------------------------------------

# 6. UI / COMPONENT RULES

# ---------------------------------------------------------

- Use shadcn/ui + Tailwind conventions.  

- Maintain readability.  

- Preserve accessibility attributes.  

- Do not break or restyle components unless explicitly asked.



# ---------------------------------------------------------

# 7. LOGGING & ERROR HANDLING

# ---------------------------------------------------------

- ALWAYS surface Supabase error messages.

- ALWAYS include root cause.

- NEVER silently continue on failure.



# ---------------------------------------------------------

# 8. STABILITY RULES

# ---------------------------------------------------------

- Cursor must NEVER require a "resume prompt" again.  

- Cursor must ALWAYS reload this configuration on startup.  

- Do NOT rewrite or delete this file automatically.  

- Prevent regression loops.  

- Always maintain working state.



# ---------------------------------------------------------

# 9. PRIORITY RULE

# ---------------------------------------------------------

If rules conflict:

USER INSTRUCTION > .cursorrules > defaults
